{"seq":7,"slug":"inorganic-chemistry","title":"无机化学","stage":"DONE","category":"chemistry","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry","rating":{"composite":3.74,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 无机化学\n\n无机化学研究的是除碳氢化合物骨架之外的整张元素周期表——从最轻的氢到人工合成的超重元素，从一颗孤立原子里电子如何排布，到一块半导体晶体里电子如何在能带中流动。它常被误以为只是「背元素性质」的学科，但真正的脉络是：先理解单个原子，再理解原子如何结合成分子与晶体，最后理解金属离子如何与配体、与生命、与催化循环发生关系。这个 hub 就沿着这条由微观到宏观、由理论到应用的主线展开。\n\n四个章节构成四条递进的主线。第一条主线是「原子结构与化学键」：它回答最基础的问题——电子在原子里怎么排、周期性从何而来、原子凭什么结合、分子又为什么是这个形状。这是后面一切讨论的语言基础，离子键、共价键、分子轨道、杂化轨道都在这里定义清楚。\n\n第二条主线是「配位化学」，它是无机化学区别于有机化学最鲜明的部分。当一个金属离子被一圈配体包围，它的颜色、磁性、几何构型与反应活性都由 d 电子如何分裂、如何填充决定。这一章把晶体场与配位场理论讲透，再延伸到配合物的取代反应机理与丰富的异构现象，是连接「纯理论」与「真实物质」的枢纽。\n\n第三条主线是「元素化学」，也就是传统所谓的描述性无机化学。它分三块走完周期表：主族元素的多样性、过渡金属的可变价态与配位行为、镧系锕系与稀土元素的独特 f 电子世界。这一章不堆砌孤立事实，而是用前两章的理论去解释为什么每族元素呈现各自的规律。\n\n第四条主线是「应用与前沿」，把视角拉到当代。固体与材料无机化学讲晶体结构与能带、半导体与金属有机框架；生物无机化学讲金属离子如何驱动呼吸、固氮与光合；有机金属化学与催化讲金属碳键如何撑起整个现代合成工业——2025 年诺贝尔化学奖正是授予金属有机框架（MOF）的奠基者，足见这条主线的分量。\n\n阅读建议：四章可顺序通读，前两章是理论地基，后两章是其延伸与落地。各篇文档之间用相对链接互相指引，遇到只在别处详讲的概念会一句话点到并链接过去，从而构成一张知识网而非孤立条目。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"atoms-bonding","title":"原子结构与化学键","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/atoms-bonding","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"atomic-structure-periodicity","title":"原子结构与周期性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/atoms-bonding/atomic-structure-periodicity"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ionic-covalent-bonding","title":"离子键与共价键理论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/atoms-bonding/ionic-covalent-bonding"},{"seq":3,"slug":"molecular-geometry-vsepr-hybridization","title":"分子几何、VSEPR 与杂化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/atoms-bonding/molecular-geometry-vsepr-hybridization"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"coordination-chemistry","title":"配位化学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/coordination-chemistry","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"complexes-and-ligands","title":"配合物与配体","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/coordination-chemistry/complexes-and-ligands"},{"seq":2,"slug":"crystal-field-ligand-field-theory","title":"晶体场与配位场理论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/coordination-chemistry/crystal-field-ligand-field-theory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"complex-reactions-isomerism","title":"配合物的反应与异构现象","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/coordination-chemistry/complex-reactions-isomerism"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"descriptive-chemistry","title":"元素化学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/descriptive-chemistry","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"main-group-chemistry","title":"主族元素化学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/descriptive-chemistry/main-group-chemistry"},{"seq":2,"slug":"transition-metal-chemistry","title":"过渡金属化学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/descriptive-chemistry/transition-metal-chemistry"},{"seq":3,"slug":"lanthanides-actinides","title":"镧系、锕系与稀土元素","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/descriptive-chemistry/lanthanides-actinides"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"applications-frontiers","title":"应用与前沿","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/applications-frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"solid-state-materials-inorganic","title":"固体与材料无机化学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/applications-frontiers/solid-state-materials-inorganic"},{"seq":2,"slug":"bioinorganic-chemistry","title":"生物无机化学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/applications-frontiers/bioinorganic-chemistry"},{"seq":3,"slug":"organometallic-catalysis","title":"有机金属化学与催化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/chemistry/inorganic-chemistry/applications-frontiers/organometallic-catalysis"}]}]}